          "text": "\n\n\n=== CURRENT ITERATION: 2 ===\n\n\n=== BOUND VARIABLES ===\n\n- `history`: `list[HistoryItem]`, read-only, 1 entry\n\nSchema:\ntype HistoryItem =\n  | { kind: \"message\", id: str, role: enum[\"user\", \"system\", \"assistant\", \"event\"], content: str, attachments?: list[HistoryAttachment] }\n  | { kind: \"lashlang_step\", id: str, protocol_iteration: int, code: str, output: list[str], images?: list[HistoryImage], error?: str | null, final_output?: any | null }\ntype HistoryAttachment = { id: str, media_type?: str | null, label?: str | null, source: str, reference: str }\ntype HistoryImage = { id: str, media_type: str, width?: int | null, height?: int | null, bytes: int, label?: str | null }\n\n\n=== FINALIZATION ===\n\nThis turn uses finish-required termination. Prose-only does not end the turn. Every non-terminal response must contain a paired `<lashlang>...</lashlang>` block that performs the next step; prose before the block is commentary/status only. Never say you will continue, inspect, patch, wait, monitor, validate, or retry unless the same response also contains the block that does it. The terminal response must be a paired `<lashlang>...</lashlang>` block that calls `finish <value>`. The value must match the REQUIRED OUTPUT contract.\n\n=== REQUIRED OUTPUT ===\n\nstr",
